[issue_comment | cfzjywxk | 2020-10-28T11:28:17Z]
The delete statement will try to lock the handleKey because the unique index has found index value. The insert statement will try to insert with the same handle key as the `delete` statement, so it's blocked. The update statement try to use the unique key to get but get nothing, so it just locks the non-exist index key with value `1, 2, 3`, thus it's not blocked.
If we change the update point get executor to use primary key which is the handle value to get we will get the conflict key.

